## Deployment notes

### What runs bare metal vs Docker

**Bare metal (systemd services):**
- Services in the hot path of every request (orchestrator, Ollama, Caddy)
- Services that benefit from direct hardware access (Ollama needs Intel Xe drivers)
- The watchdog (zero dependencies, must survive Docker failures)
- Services that manage persistent long-lived state (claude-mem worker)

**Docker containers:**
- MCP servers (isolation from untrusted external data parsing)
- Paperclip (Phase 4+, convenient packaging)
- Things that might crash and need fresh restart

### Port allocation

| Port | Service |
|------|---------|
| 22 | SSH (Tailscale-authenticated) |
| 443 | Caddy HTTPS (public via Tailscale) |
| 8000 | FastAPI orchestrator (localhost only, behind Caddy) |
| 11434 | Ollama (localhost only) |
| 37777 | claude-mem worker (localhost only) |
| 3100 | Paperclip (Phase 4+, localhost) |

Only 22 and 443 are exposed through Tailscale. Everything else is localhost-only.

### Filesystem layout

All writable state inside LUKS-encrypted partition. Key locations:
- `/home/nova/genesis/` — public repo working copy
- `/home/nova/genesis-config/` — private repo working copy (git-crypt)
- `/var/lib/genesis/` — SQLite databases and message bus staging
- `/home/nova/.claude/` — Claude Code state, per-agent CLAUDE.md
- `/home/nova/.claude-mem/` — claude-mem SQLite + observations
- `/home/nova/.ollama/` — Qwen 3B model weights

Backups snapshot `/var/lib/genesis/` and `/home/nova/.claude-mem/` every 6 hours to Google Drive (encrypted via rclone crypt).
